Sec. 30001. This section amends the Consumer Financial Protection Act of 2010 to reduce the annual funding cap for the Bureau of Consumer Financial Protection. Specifically, it strikes the existing cap of 12 percent of the Federal Reserve Board’s budget and inserts a new cap of 6.5 percent.

Sec. 30002. This section rescinds all unobligated balances of funds previously made available for the Green and Resilient Retrofit Program for Multifamily Housing. These funds were originally appropriated under section 30002(a) of the Inflation Reduction Act (Public Law 117-169).

Sec. 30003. This section eliminates the Securities and Exchange Commission Reserve Fund by striking the relevant subsection from the Securities Exchange Act of 1934. It mandates that any remaining obligated and unobligated balances in the fund be transferred to the general fund of the Treasury effective October 1, 2025. The SEC is permitted to expend previously obligated amounts for ongoing activities until that transfer date.

Sec. 30004. This section appropriates $1,000,000,000 from amounts not otherwise appropriated for fiscal year 2025 to carry out the Defense Production Act. These funds will remain available for obligation until September 30, 2027. [end of text]


